# Project context lives in `context/`

This repository carries its own AI memory so work survives switching between
assistants, accounts, and tools. Full rules: [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md).
Full procedure: [SPEC.md](mdc:context/_meta/SPEC.md).

## At the start of a session

Read [CURRENT.md](mdc:context/CURRENT.md) **first**. It states the project, the
current objective, what has been decided, where the work stands, and what to do
next — without any chat history.

Then as needed: [TASKS.md](mdc:context/TASKS.md) for the queue and open questions,
[DECISIONS.md](mdc:context/DECISIONS.md) for binding constraints,
[LESSONS.md](mdc:context/LESSONS.md) **before proposing an approach** (it lists
what already failed), [PROJECT.md](mdc:context/PROJECT.md) for the stack and
conventions.

Confidence tags: `[FACT]` verified · `[DECIDED]` binding · `[ASSUMED]`
unconfirmed · `[UNVERIFIED]` unchecked · `[OPEN]` unanswered. Anything `[ASSUMED]`
or `[UNVERIFIED]` is not established — verify it or say you did not. Where the
repo and the context disagree, the repo is right and the context is stale.

Do not ask the user to re-explain anything `context/` already answers.

## When asked to save or checkpoint the context

Follow [SPEC.md](mdc:context/_meta/SPEC.md) §4. Summary:

1. Extract high-signal information from this conversation — decisions **with
   reasoning**, changes with paths, status, failed approaches, open questions,
   assumptions, preferences, environment, commands.
2. **Read the existing `context/` files before writing.** Never write blind.
3. Merge: append new, update changed, and **supersede contradictions rather than
   overwriting** — mark the old entry `SUPERSEDED by D-###` and keep its text.
4. Rewrite `CURRENT.md` under 400 lines; anything you remove must first exist in a
   longer-lived file.
5. Append to `HISTORY.md`, write `context/sessions/YYYY-MM-DD-NN-slug.md`, update
   `context/_meta/state.json`.
6. If nothing material changed, write nothing and say so.

Never record secrets — note that a credential exists and where it lives, never its
value.

## Naming trap

`QuizApp` (new system), `QuizApp-9AMM` (legacy MVC 4), and `QuickBuzz` (legacy
buzzer) are three different things. Check `context/PROJECT.md` §Domain glossary
before editing, or you will change the wrong system.
